@startuml deployment
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Deployment — one image, three exposure problems

header
<b>One image.</b>  The entrypoint takes a service name, so Kubernetes runs <b>args: ["text"]</b> and compose runs <b>command: text</b>.
Twenty-four Dockerfiles would be twenty-four things to keep in sync, and it makes <b>--all-in-one</b> an argument rather than a build.
endheader

actor "legacy Mumble\nclient" as legacy #EEEEEE
actor "Fancy client" as fancy #E3F2FD

package "cluster" as K8S #F5F5F5 {

  node "**Service: LoadBalancer**\n**TCP** 64738\n«NOT an Ingress»" as lbtcp #FFCDD2
  node "**Service: LoadBalancer**\n**UDP** 64738\n**NOT** sessionAffinity: ClientIP" as lbudp #FFCDD2
  node "**Ingress**\nHTTPS\n«the only one that fits»" as ing #C8E6C9

  node "**gateway** pods\nreplicas: N\nstateful per connection,\n**but resumable elsewhere**" as gwpod #FFE9D6
  node "**session store**\nsequence + replay buffer\noutlives any gateway pod" as sstore #FFE0B2
  node "**voice** pods\nreplicas: N\nholds ciphers + membership cache" as vpod #FFF8E1
  node "**files/http** pods\nstateless" as fpod #E8F5E9
  node "**essential** pods\nsession · permissions\nmetadata · userdata" as epod #FFEBEE
  node "**optional** pods\npush · audit · polls · …" as opod #E8F5E9
}

legacy --> lbtcp
fancy  --> lbtcp
lbtcp  --> gwpod

legacy --> lbudp
fancy  --> lbudp
lbudp  --> vpod

fancy --> ing
ing   --> fpod

gwpod -[#1565C0]-> epod : gRPC + circuit breaker
gwpod -[#1565C0]-> opod : gRPC
gwpod -[#1565C0]-> vpod : gRPC\n(signalling + UDPTunnel only)
gwpod -[#1565C0]-> sstore : sequence + replay
vpod  -[#1565C0].-> epod : membership snapshot

note right of sstore #FFE0B2
  **Problem 4: RESUME, or a rolling deploy is a DDoS.**
  Drain a gateway pod holding 10 000 clients and all of
  them reconnect and pull a full flood of every
  ChannelState and UserState at once, into metadata and
  session-view, simultaneously.
  With sequence numbers a client replays only the gap -
  but the sequence and its replay buffer must **outlive the pod**,
  or a resuming client landing on a different pod has nothing
  to resume against.
  Legacy clients cannot resume. They get the full flood,
  so stagger readiness and send a jittered reconnect hint.
end note

note right of lbtcp #FFCDD2
  **Problem 1: the gateway cannot use an Ingress.**
  Kubernetes `Ingress` is HTTP/HTTPS only, and Mumble is
  raw TCP+TLS. It needs `Service type=LoadBalancer`, or
  Gateway API `TCPRoute`.
  This is also why the component is called the **gateway**
  and not `ingress` - naming it after a resource it can
  never use is a trap waiting for the next person.
end note

note right of lbudp #FFCDD2
  **Problem 2: client affinity is the wrong affinity.**
  Audio routing is **per channel**, so a channel's members must
  share a voice pod. `sessionAffinity: ClientIP` pins each
  *client* — which scatters a channel across pods, and there is
  **no inter-pod audio path** in this design. It makes things
  worse, not better.
  Discord assigns a voice *channel* to a voice server and **tells**
  the client which one. Mumble has no such field, and
  **a legacy client sends UDP to the port it made TCP to** —
  so it cannot be redirected.
  So, in order of increasing capability:
  · **one voice pod per virtual server** - vertical only, honest
  · **a forwarding mesh between pods** - scales, costs a hop
  · **shard by channel + an explicit endpoint in `ServerSync`** for
    Fancy clients; legacy stays on the advertised pod
  See scaling.puml.
end note

note bottom of vpod #FFF8E1
  **Problem 3: a restarted voice pod has cold caches.**
  It holds ciphers and a membership cache, neither of which
  survives. Audio arriving before it re-subscribes is dropped
  with nothing to show for it.
  So `/readyz` must gate on **cache warm-up**, not on the
  process being alive - and it must be a *different* endpoint
  from `/healthz`, or Kubernetes will route to a cold pod.
end note

note bottom of ing #C8E6C9
  files/http is the only component speaking HTTP, so it is
  the only one that gets TLS termination, an Ingress and a
  CDN for free. That is the whole reason bulk transfer was
  moved off the control stream.
end note

note as COMPOSE #FFFFFF
  **docker compose** is the same picture with the load
  balancers replaced by published ports, and voice
  co-located with the gateway so legacy UDP lands right.
  **--all-in-one** collapses every pod into one container:
  same binary, same TOML, gRPC replaced by in-process calls.
end note

@enduml
